    {
      "text": "Table 1: A tale of three distributions; comparing properties across offline RL methods.",
      "bbox": [
        83.36900329589844,
        233.44850158691406,
        453.12847900390625,
        241.46446228027344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The methods we",
      "bbox": [
        461.36474609375,
        233.547119140625,
        528.2822265625,
        241.46446228027344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mention are defined as follows: MOREL etc. Kidambi et al. (2020); Yu et al. (2020; 2021); Rigter et al. (2022),",
      "bbox": [
        83.70099639892578,
        244.50616455078125,
        529.6659545898438,
        252.4235076904297
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Dreamer Hafner et al. (2020), DWMS (Diffusion World Models) Alonso et al. (2023), UniSim Yang et al. (2024),",
      "bbox": [
        83.70099639892578,
        255.3665313720703,
        529.6444702148438,
        263.3824768066406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SynthER Lu et al. (2024), DWM (Diffusion World Model) Ding et al. (2024), PolyGRAD Rigter et al. (2024),",
      "bbox": [
        83.70099639892578,
        266.42413330078125,
        529.6787719726562,
        274.3414611816406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PGD (Policy-Guided Diffusion) Jackson et al. (2024), Diffuser Janner et al. (2022), DT (decision transformer)",
      "bbox": [
        83.70099639892578,
        277.38214111328125,
        529.4625854492188,
        285.2994689941406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chen et al. (2021), TT (trajectory transformer) Janner et al. (2021), BC (behavior cloning), CQL (conservative",
      "bbox": [
        83.70099639892578,
        288.3411560058594,
        528.3506469726562,
        296.25848388671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Q learning) Kumar et al. (2020), IQL (implicit Q learning) Kostrikov et al. (2021), DD (Decision Diffuser)",
      "bbox": [
        83.70099639892578,
        299.3001403808594,
        529.4638061523438,
        307.21746826171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ajay et al. (2023), DP (Diffuson Policy) Chi et al. (2023), IH (Imitiating Humans) Pearce et al. (2023) DBC",
      "bbox": [
        83.36000061035156,
        310.2591552734375,
        528.3948974609375,
        318.1764831542969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(Diffusion BC) Wang et al. (2023) .",
      "bbox": [
        82.62300109863281,
        321.2181396484375,
        226.0675048828125,
        329.1354675292969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a simple sampling-based planner that does not rely on classifier guidance. Other works using MS with a joint",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        381.1689147949219,
        540.4847412109375,
        391.13153076171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "proposal are decision transformer (DT) (Chen et al., 2021), and trajectory transformer (Janner et al., 2021).",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        393.1249084472656,
        542.129638671875,
        403.0875244140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Similarly, the “Decision Diffuser” paper (Ajay et al., 2023) learns a trajectory distribution over states, and",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        411.0569152832031,
        540.219482421875,
        421.01953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "uses classifier-free guidance to generate trajectories that have high predicted reward; the state sequence is",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        423.0129089355469,
        540.2886962890625,
        432.97552490234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "then converted into an action sequence using a separately trained inverse dynamics model (IDM). However,",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        434.9678955078125,
        541.625244140625,
        444.9305114746094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "this approach does not allow for run-time specification of new reward functions.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        446.92291259765625,
        420.6610412597656,
        456.8855285644531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "MPC has also been applied in model-based RL, with TD-MPC (Hansen et al., 2022) and TD-MPC2 (Hansen",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        464.85589599609375,
        540.152587890625,
        474.8185119628906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "et al., 2023) being the representative methods. D-MPC differs from the TD-MPC line of work in that D-MPC",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
