      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "uses multi-step diffusion models for both action proposal and dynamics model, while the TD-MPC line of work",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        488.7658996582031,
        540.4456176757812,
        498.728515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "uses single-step MLPs. In addition, the TD-MPC line of work focuses on online learning with environment",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        500.7209167480469,
        540.4862060546875,
        510.68353271484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "interactions while in D-MPC we focus on learning from offline data and then use the learned models for doing",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        512.6759033203125,
        540.2113647460938,
        522.6384887695312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "MPC in the environment.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        524.6309204101562,
        184.0194854736328,
        534.593505859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The model-based offline planning or MBOP paper (Argenson & Dulac-Arnold, 2021) was the original",
      "bbox": [
        71.64099884033203,
        542.5639038085938,
        540.16357421875,
        552.5264892578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "inspiration for our method. In contrast with the previous MPC methods, it factorizes the dynamics models",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        554.5189208984375,
        540.2120361328125,
        564.4815063476562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and the action proposal model, which are learned separately and used at planning to optimize for novel",
      "bbox": [
