        576.4375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "rewards. The main difference with our work is that they use ensembles of one-step deterministic MLPs for",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        578.429931640625,
        540.4232177734375,
        588.3925170898438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "their dynamics models and action models, whereas we use a single stochastic trajectory level diffusion model.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        590.3848876953125,
        542.1615600585938,
        600.3474731445312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In addition they use a somewhat complex trajectory optimization method for the action selection, whereas",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        602.3399047851562,
        540.200439453125,
        612.302490234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "we use a simple sampling-based planner. Finally, we also study adapting the model to novel dynamics.",
      "bbox": [
        71.64099884033203,
        614.294921875,
        520.4261474609375,
        624.2575073242188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Several recent works are closely related to D-MPC. “Model-based Diffusion\" (MBD) (Pan et al., 2024) also",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        632.2279052734375,
        540.1845092773438,
        642.1904907226562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "utilizes diffusion for trajectory-level search, but it assumes known environment dynamics, unlike our setting.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        644.1829223632812,
        542.177978515625,
        654.1455078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "“DyDiff\" Zhao et al. (2024) employs a diffusion-based dynamics model with a structure similar to D-MPC’s,",
      "bbox": [
